But today we are talking about episode, what episode is this episode?
不过今天我们要说的是剧集，这一集是哪一集呢？

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:18.969
Episode eight, it's called Atlantic City.
第八集，它叫大西洋城。

00:01:18.969 --> 00:01:21.290
It was written by...
它是由...写的

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:30.409
This was written by Maria Ferrari, who was our writer's assistant at the time, and he went on to become a writer on How Much Mother, and has gone on to a bunch of really cool things since then.
这是玛丽亚·法拉利（Maria Ferrari）写的，她当时是我们作家的助理，后来他成为了《How Much Mother》的作家，从那时起，他又创作了很多非常酷的东西。

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:34.370
And she wrote this one, I think this was her first episode, I think.
她写了这个，我想这是她的第一集。

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:36.370
Boy, no, wait, there may have been one in season one.
天哪，不，等等，第一季可能就有一个。

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.209
I'm having a moment.
我有一会儿。

00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:40.209
You were just talking about Waldo Regading and this is just proof of it.
你刚才谈论的是沃尔多·雷加丁，这只是证明。

00:01:40.209 --> 00:01:41.650
But it's a huge thing.
但这是一件大事。

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:49.129
You remember what we were talking about Courtney had, Courtney Kang had been on like four different shows that all got canceled before her episode aired.
你还记得我们谈论的考特尼，考特尼康参加过四场不同的节目，但在她的剧集播出之前全部被取消。

00:01:49.129 --> 00:01:55.689
So I think return to the shirt, right, was her first episode from season one that had ever made it onto the air.
所以我认为《回归衬衫》是她第一季播出的第一集。

00:01:55.689 --> 00:02:08.449
I mean, there's a weird thing in Hollywood where you can be like shooting pilots and shooting episodes of canceled shows and no one ever see, you can't tell your hometown friends like, here's my episode, or I'm gonna be on TV, but you're working.
我的意思是，在好莱坞有一件奇怪的事情，你可以像拍摄试播集和拍摄被取消的节目的剧集一样，却没有人看到，你不能告诉你家乡的朋友，比如，这是我的剧集，或者我要上电视，但你在工作。

00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:09.710
You're like getting your health insurance.
您就像获得健康保险一样。

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.729
You're working in Hollywood.
你在好莱坞工作。

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:12.930
It's weird.
很奇怪。

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.009
It used to be a very, that part's weird.
这曾经是一个非常非常奇怪的部分。

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:30.810
Another part that's gotten even weirder is becoming a writer's assistant and our script coordinator, that little mini department in the writing department of a TV show, that used to be kind of the most logical way to become a writer, right?
另一部分变得更奇怪的是成为作家助理和我们的剧本协调员，电视节目写作部门的一个小部门，这曾经是成为作家最合乎逻辑的方式，对吗？

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:49.289
Every other way requires some bit of magic or miracle, But the work your way up way is to get in a writer's room and be in there and learn and soak things up and hope that you get an opportunity to write a script on that show and move into being a writer maybe on that show or another show, your next show, past it, you're gonna be a writer on that show.
其他的方式都需要一些魔法或奇迹，但你的晋升之路的工作是进入编剧的房间，在那里学习和吸收东西，并希望你有机会写那个节目的剧本，并成为一名编剧，也许在那个节目或另一个节目，你的下一个节目，过去了，你将成为那个节目的作家。

00:02:49.289 --> 00:02:52.009
It has gotten so hard to do that now.
现在要做到这一点已经很难了。

00:02:52.009 --> 00:03:00.770
There are so few shows, the rooms have gotten so small, the episode orders of TV shows, like these little streaming shows or eight episodes, 10 episodes, so small.
节目太少了，房间太小了，电视剧的集数顺序，像这些小节目或者八集、十集，那么小。

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:11.590
So it was already really hard to do when writers on our show like Matt Coon and Maria Ferrari, Jenny Hendricks, like writers assistants had graduated to then write himium episodes and get on staff.
因此，当我们节目中的编剧，如马特·库恩、玛丽亚·法拉利、珍妮·亨德里克斯、编剧助理等毕业后开始写剧集并加入工作人员时，这已经很难了。

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:14.449
That was pretty hard to do 20 years ago.
这在20年前是很难做到的。

00:03:14.449 --> 00:03:17.129
It's exponentially harder to do now.
现在要做起来要困难得多。

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:20.650
It really is, we get asked Carter and I all the time, like, well, what's the path?
确实如此，卡特和我总是被问到，嗯，那条路是什么？

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.370
And we're like, it started off hard and it got harder.
我们就像，一开始很艰难，然后变得越来越困难。

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.210
So God bless you if you're out there, do it.
所以，如果你在外面，上帝保佑你，那就去做吧。

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.689
If you can get into a room and be a writers assistant, still a great way to do it.
如果你能进入一个房间并成为一名作家助理，这仍然是一个很好的方式。

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:33.129
But there aren't as many 22 episode opportunities to do that.
但 22 集的机会并不多。

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.849
Well, it's hard, I think, to reinvent the wheel.
嗯，我认为重新发明轮子很难。

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:40.650
I think that a lot of times we try to pull apart television or pull apart the model of how things have been done.
我认为很多时候我们试图分解电视或分解事物的运作模式。

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.689
And for a while, it looks like, oh, we discovered a new way.
有一段时间，我们似乎发现了一种新方法。

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:51.409
But what you're seeing is all these different streamers, all the now they have ads, now they're not doing them.
但你看到的是所有这些不同的流媒体，现在他们都有广告，现在他们不做广告。

00:03:51.409 --> 00:03:53.569
They're not dropping all the episodes or doing it once a week.
他们不会放弃所有剧集或每周播放一次。

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:55.569
It's like they're inventing television.
就像他们正在发明电视一样。

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:57.370
They're bundling the streamers together.
他们正在将彩带捆绑在一起。

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.770
Suddenly, you have cable.
突然间，你有了电缆。

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.770
It's ridiculous.
这太荒谬了。

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.289
they're just going back to the model of, because there was something satisfying up there.
他们只是回到了模型，因为那里有一些令人满意的东西。

00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:19.970
I think the reason everyone freaked out over the pit was not just because it was a great show, which it was, it was because it was an old model, dusted off and made new again, but it was like every week, a procedure, following a group of people in a workplace, like there was just something very satisfying about it.
我认为每个人都对这个坑感到惊慌的原因不仅仅是因为它是一场精彩的表演，确实如此，而是因为它是一个旧模型，除尘并重新焕然一新，但它就像每周，一个程序，在工作场所跟踪一群人，就像有一些非常令人满意的东西。

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:29.009
And I think like we can try to reinvent the wheel, but ultimately like, I think they did crack the code of what makes TV work, and we're just gonna come back to it, hopefully.
我认为我们可以尝试重新发明轮子，但最终，我认为他们确实破解了电视运作的密码，希望我们能回到它。

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:29.850
Yeah.
是的。

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.529
And podcasting is radio.
播客是广播。

00:04:31.529 --> 00:04:34.329
Like we've put new names, we've put new, we're doing a radio show.
就像我们换了新名字一样，我们换了新名字，我们正在做一个广播节目。

00:04:34.329 --> 00:04:35.250
That's what we're doing.
这就是我们正在做的事情。

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.329
Like we're just slapping names on shit.
就像我们只是在给狗屎打名字一样。

00:04:37.329 --> 00:04:38.610
Like it's new, it's not new.
就像是新的一样，它并不新鲜。

