卡特，我只是觉得，有更多的吸烟夹克，雪茄，一种老式的，你知道我的意思吗？

00:51:37.809 --> 00:51:42.929
He's got this kind of like, he's a little more in those, right?
他有这样的风格，他还有更多这样的风格，对吧？

00:51:42.929 --> 00:51:48.170
He likes, I think he likes every now and again, sort of being like that, but he's not really, he's not smoking cigars.
他喜欢，我想他时不时地喜欢这样，但他不是真的，他不抽雪茄。

00:51:48.170 --> 00:51:57.090
Through the whole run of the show, whenever we smoked cigars, 9.30 in the morning, it was always, never at night, it was always so early.
在整个演出过程中，每当我们抽雪茄时，早上9.30，总是，从来没有在晚上，总是那么早。

00:51:57.090 --> 00:52:05.889
And Dave Baker was good at smoking cigars, and Neil was actually quite good at smoking cigars and better than me, but I would always have to say, Dave, show me again, like I just wasn't.
戴夫·贝克（Dave Baker）很擅长抽雪茄，而尼尔（Neil）实际上也很擅长抽雪茄，而且比我更好，但我总是不得不说，戴夫（Dave），再给我看一次，就像我不是一样。

00:52:05.889 --> 00:52:07.650
It's like a life, that's something, it's a life choice.
这就像一种生活，那是一种东西，这是一种生活的选择。

00:52:07.650 --> 00:52:14.210
You're either a guy who decides to really learn that and really look okay doing it or you're, there's no middle ground, I feel.
你要么是一个决定真正学习这一点并且看起来确实做得很好的人，要么你是，我觉得没有中间立场。

00:52:14.210 --> 00:52:15.489
And I never really learned how to do it.
我从来没有真正学会如何去做。

00:52:15.489 --> 00:52:18.170
You probably had to cut away when I was smoking the cigars.
当我抽雪茄的时候你可能不得不把它切掉。

00:52:18.170 --> 00:52:20.010
It's not my great talent.
这不是我的伟大才能。

00:52:20.010 --> 00:52:25.530
I would say that as a category, the number one type of question we get is about improv.
我想说，作为一个类别，我们收到的第一类问题是关于即兴创作的。

00:52:25.530 --> 00:52:27.650
And we've talked about this a lot.
我们已经讨论过很多次了。

00:52:27.650 --> 00:52:30.329
We have clarified, you have clarified.
我们已经澄清了，你也已经澄清了。

00:52:30.329 --> 00:52:32.389
The show is not improvised.
该节目并非即兴表演。

00:52:32.389 --> 00:52:35.730
We've talked about Josh's great and mailed it.
我们已经谈论了乔什的伟大并邮寄了它。

00:52:35.730 --> 00:52:37.889
And- There was some.
而且——有一些。

00:52:37.889 --> 00:52:40.130
I mean, there was some- And the idea that there were some.
我的意思是，有一些——以及有一些的想法。

00:52:40.130 --> 00:52:43.250
I mean, the way this question was asked, actually by Jessica, yeah, hi, Jessica.
我的意思是，这个问题实际上是由杰西卡提出的，是的，嗨，杰西卡。

00:52:43.250 --> 00:52:49.690
Is the game scene improv to make things as confusing as possible or was it all scripted out?
游戏场景是为了让事情变得尽可能混乱而进行的即兴创作还是全部都是按剧本编写的？

00:52:49.690 --> 00:52:53.170
No, you can only make it insane if you plan it.
不，如果你有计划的话，你只能让它变得疯狂。

00:52:53.170 --> 00:52:56.210
It has to be very meticulously planned to make no sense.
它必须非常仔细地计划才没有任何意义。

00:52:56.210 --> 00:52:57.969
That's the paradise.
那就是天堂。

00:52:57.969 --> 00:53:03.530
Because everyone, everyone playing it is unified in terms of knowing the rules.
因为每个人、每个玩它的人在了解规则方面都是统一的。

00:53:03.530 --> 00:53:05.489
The order of events has to be in stone.
事件的顺序必须是一成不变的。

00:53:05.489 --> 00:53:15.909
I will say, Alec, I think that this question is a compliment, which means there's something that feels very lifelike and spontaneous about the show.
我会说，亚历克，我认为这个问题是一种恭维，这意味着这部剧有一些感觉非常逼真和自发。

00:53:15.909 --> 00:53:23.309
But the reason, like Craig is saying, like the reason it feels that way is because it's quite well mapped.
但正如克雷格所说，之所以会有这种感觉，是因为它的地图绘制得非常好。

00:53:23.309 --> 00:53:24.150
Yeah.
是的。

00:53:24.150 --> 00:53:24.989
You know.
你知道。

00:53:24.989 --> 00:53:25.829
It's a compliment to the cast.
这是对演员阵容的赞扬。

00:53:25.829 --> 00:53:30.550
Cause you make it seem very naturalistic and the truth is there wasn't much improv.
因为你让它看起来非常自然，而事实是没有太多即兴发挥。

00:53:30.550 --> 00:53:38.426
Like we were just, we had, we had Cobion a few episodes ago talking about slap bed and the very ending of that episode where the whole gang is watching the video, the music video on Barney's laptop.
就像我们刚才那样，我们在几集前就让 Cobion 谈论了拍打床，以及那一集的结尾，整个团伙都在观看视频，巴尼笔记本电脑上的音乐视频。

00:53:38.426 --> 00:53:40.932
I remember that was like, you guys were riffing a little there.
我记得那就像，你们在那里即兴演奏了一点。

00:53:40.932 --> 00:53:45.029
Like, I think we fed you some lines and you were riffing and that had a little bit of a different feel.
就像，我想我们给你提供了一些台词，你在即兴演奏，这有一点不同的感觉。

00:53:45.030 --> 00:53:46.313
But that's, that's rare.
但就是这样，很少见。

00:53:46.313 --> 00:53:47.115
It's very rare.
这是非常罕见的。

00:53:47.115 --> 00:53:53.693
And to make something as stupid as that intricate gambling game that makes no sense, so much work in planning goes in that.
为了制作像那种复杂的毫无意义的赌博游戏这样愚蠢的东西，需要花费大量的规划工作。

00:53:53.693 --> 00:53:55.030
That's my favorite thing.
这是我最喜欢的事情。

00:53:55.030 --> 00:53:59.115
how much work goes into creating something super, super stupid.
创造出超级、超级愚蠢的东西需要付出多少努力。

00:53:59.115 --> 00:54:02.293
That is one of my favorite just brands of comedy.
这是我最喜欢的喜剧品牌之一。

00:54:02.293 --> 00:54:07.741
But when something feels chaotic and insane, usually a lot of planning went into it.
但当某件事让人感觉混乱和疯狂时，通常会进行很多计划。

00:54:07.741 --> 00:54:18.765
It just seems like, I mean, no show really in the, your Euro is sort of when that notion started, that there might be a lot anywhere from a little bit to a lot of improv.
我的意思是，当这个概念开始时，欧元似乎并没有真正表现出来，可能会有很多改进，从一点点到很多。

00:54:18.765 --> 00:54:34.006
I think we got out the idea that in the office, certainly when you go and you watch the outtakes, it seems like Steve Carell is making up a lot of stuff as he's going on to just keep going and keep going and keep going with that style.
我认为我们得到了这样的想法：在办公室里，当然，当你去观看剪辑时，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔似乎正在编造很多东西，因为他将继续以这种风格继续前进。

00:54:34.006 --> 00:54:36.730
But this stuff is pretty tightly scripted.
但这东西的脚本非常严格。

00:54:36.730 --> 00:54:40.306
We had to shoot in three days, you know, the office is probably a five day shoot.
我们必须在三天内拍摄，你知道，办公室可能需要五天的拍摄。

00:54:40.306 --> 00:54:42.160
And even that they would have to limit it.
即使如此，他们也必须限制它。

00:54:42.160 --> 00:54:46.929
Like these movies like Judd Apatow movies and movies were like, Oh, the actors just go and go and go and go.
就像贾德·阿帕图这样的电影一样，哦，演员们就这样走啊走啊走啊。

00:54:46.929 --> 00:54:48.210
You just can't do that in TV.
你在电视上做不到这一点。

00:54:48.210 --> 00:54:49.388
There's just no time.
只是没有时间。

00:54:49.388 --> 00:54:52.981
You have to finish shooting, edit it and get it on TV in a week.
你必须在一周内完成拍摄、剪辑并在电视上播出。

00:54:52.981 --> 00:54:54.889
Like it's there's not enough time.
好像时间不够。

00:54:54.889 --> 00:54:59.170
And because of the way the show was structured, it's just so intricate.
由于节目的结构方式，它非常复杂。

00:54:59.170 --> 00:55:04.610
It's just, it's not a lazy porch, you know, shooting the shit kind of show.
只是，这不是一个懒惰的门廊，你知道，拍摄那种糟糕的节目。

00:55:04.610 --> 00:55:07.869
It's like, you know, you have 40 to 60 scenes, you gotta move.
就像，你知道，你有 40 到 60 个场景，你必须移动。

00:55:07.869 --> 00:55:08.710
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:08.710 --> 00:55:10.489
Let's see what we come up with on the fly.
让我们看看我们即时想到了什么。

00:55:10.489 --> 00:55:11.690
It's, you can't do it.
是的，你做不到。

00:55:11.690 --> 00:55:13.409
You have 10 minutes to shoot all the scene.
您有 10 分钟时间拍摄所有场景。

00:55:13.409 --> 00:55:27.039
Well, just as a last question here, Terry ODO2 just wants to point out how great the song sync to the bottom with you was just want to talk a little more about that music choice as we end this episode.
好吧，就像这里的最后一个问题，Terry ODO2 只是想指出这首歌与你的底部同步有多棒，只是想在我们结束这一集时更多地谈论一下音乐选择。

00:55:27.039 --> 00:55:27.539
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:27.539 --> 00:55:28.039
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:28.039 --> 00:55:28.539
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:28.539 --> 00:55:29.691
I was so excited.
我很兴奋。

00:55:29.691 --> 00:55:31.183
That was, that was me.
那就是，那就是我。

00:55:31.183 --> 00:55:34.167
That was my choice because I love that song.
这是我的选择，因为我喜欢那首歌。

00:55:34.167 --> 00:55:35.252
I love that man.
我爱那个男人。

00:55:35.252 --> 00:55:38.099
Fountains of Wayne, Adam Schausinger, RIP.
韦恩喷泉，亚当·绍辛格，安息吧。

00:55:38.099 --> 00:55:40.812
Very, very sadly, lost him during COVID.
非常非常悲伤，在新冠疫情期间失去了他。

00:55:40.812 --> 00:55:43.321
Such a talented, brilliant, melodist.
这样一位才华横溢、才华横溢、才华横溢的旋律家。

00:55:43.321 --> 00:55:44.338
Is that a word?
这是一个词吗？

00:55:44.338 --> 00:55:44.948
Melodist?
旋律师？

00:55:44.948 --> 00:55:50.372
The melody writer, he's just like, he is, he is a Beatles caliber melody writer.
旋律作者，他就像，他是，他是披头士乐队级别的旋律作者。

00:55:49.889 --> 00:55:52.289
And they were says, founds of Wayne, such a great band.
据说他们是韦恩这样一支伟大乐队的创始人。

00:55:52.769 --> 00:55:56.369
And yeah, I was just a huge fan of that song.
是的，我只是那首歌的超级粉丝。

00:55:56.369 --> 00:55:57.010
I love that song.
我喜欢那首歌。

00:55:57.010 --> 00:55:59.369
I play that guitar a little bit and play for my son and stuff.
我会弹一点吉他，为我的儿子和其他人弹奏。

00:55:59.369 --> 00:56:01.570
And we, it just felt like it fit.
而我们，感觉很合适。

00:56:01.570 --> 00:56:03.090
It's like this tortured love song, right?
就像这首折磨人的情歌，对吧？

00:56:03.090 --> 00:56:11.809
It's at this moment where Marshall and Lily are saying, let's crawl through the Shawshank sewer pipe of our judgmental family's eyes.
就在这个时候，马歇尔和莉莉说，让我们从我们挑剔的家庭眼睛里的肖申克下水道里爬过去吧。

00:56:12.170 --> 00:56:14.250
And let's go through all the things we're dodging.
让我们回顾一下我们正在回避的所有事情。

00:56:14.250 --> 00:56:22.741
like, we'll go through this crucible of all of Marshall's family is going to think Lily's the runaway bride and scowl at her for breaking Marshall's heart a few months back.
就像，我们将经历马歇尔所有家人的严酷考验，他们会认为莉莉是离家出走的新娘，并对她几个月前伤了马歇尔的心感到愤怒。

00:56:22.741 --> 00:56:26.815
And she says, let's do it anyway, because that's, that's how we really get married.
她说，无论如何，我们就这么做吧，因为那就是我们真正结婚的方式。

00:56:26.815 --> 00:56:28.925
And that song, sink to the bottom with you.
还有那首歌，与你一起沉入谷底。

00:56:28.925 --> 00:56:30.643
I will sink to the bottom with you.
我会和你一起沉入海底。

00:56:30.643 --> 00:56:36.189
I will go in with you, even if it might mean we were going to go all the way to the bottom of the ocean together.
我会和你一起进去，即使这可能意味着我们要一起一直走到海底。

00:56:36.189 --> 00:56:37.024
I'll still do it.
我还是会做。

00:56:37.024 --> 00:56:40.999
It just, it feels like it fit the tone of like, sometimes that's marriage, right?
只是，感觉这很符合这样的语气，有时这就是婚姻，对吧？

00:56:40.999 --> 00:56:42.374
Sometimes that's couplehood.
有时这就是夫妻关系。

00:56:42.374 --> 00:56:44.680
You got to sort of sink to the bottom together.
你们必须一起沉入海底。

00:56:44.680 --> 00:56:47.036
So I was really happy to get that song on there.
所以我真的很高兴能把这首歌放在那里。

00:56:47.036 --> 00:56:51.405
And it had really moved me hearing it again for the first time since Adam Sussinger died.
自从亚当·苏辛格（Adam Sussinger）去世后，我第一次再次听到这句话，真的让我很感动。

00:56:51.405 --> 00:56:52.828
And yeah, just what a talent.
是的，真是一个天才。

00:56:52.828 --> 00:56:54.889
So it was great to get his music on there.
所以很高兴能在那里播放他的音乐。

00:56:55.929 --> 00:57:00.845
Craig, it's always such a pleasure to dive into these episodes with you.
克雷格，很高兴和你一起深入了解这些剧集。

00:57:00.845 --> 00:57:02.005
Alec, Doug, Alex.
亚历克、道格、亚历克斯。

00:57:02.005 --> 00:57:03.097
I love you guys.
我爱你们。

00:57:03.097 --> 00:57:12.449
It really does have the feeling of like looking through an old photo album and and be like, oh my God, I totally forgot about that night.
它确实有一种感觉就像翻阅一本旧相册，然后说，天哪，我完全忘记了那天晚上。

00:57:12.449 --> 00:57:13.989
That was insane, you know?
那太疯狂了，你知道吗？

00:57:13.989 --> 00:57:17.289
It's really like, it's such a fun stroll down memory lane.
真的，沿着记忆的小巷漫步真是太有趣了。

00:57:17.289 --> 00:57:27.469
And not many people have this much of their, you know, 30s document, like this was before everyone started recording everything.
没有多少人有这么多 30 多岁的文件，就像每个人都开始记录一切之前的那样。

00:57:27.469 --> 00:57:33.550
Like we really do have this living photo album of us at a time in our lives that it's pretty extraordinary.
就像我们确实拥有我们生命中某个时刻的活生生相册一样，它非常非凡。

00:57:33.550 --> 00:57:36.630
And it looks great at the ending of that episode.
那集的结尾看起来很棒。

00:57:36.630 --> 00:57:39.750
It's all of them out on this boat with the sun setting over the horizon.
他们所有人都在这艘船上，夕阳西下。

00:57:39.750 --> 00:57:42.070
Of course, it's just, it's a really good blue screen.
当然，只是，这是一个非常好的蓝屏。

00:57:42.070 --> 00:57:44.469
It's obviously, it's just, it's beautifully done.
显然，这只是，做得很漂亮。

00:57:44.469 --> 00:57:47.710
Like, our team is amazing to make that look that good.
就像，我们的团队非常出色，能够让它看起来那么好。

00:57:48.909 --> 00:57:58.349
In the production point and in post, it looked like a really beautiful moment with all of these guys floating out on the Atlantic Ocean and with the sun setting, and it really works.
在制作点和后期，所有这些人都漂浮在大西洋上，伴随着夕阳西下，这看起来真的是一个非常美丽的时刻，而且它真的很有效。

00:57:58.349 --> 00:57:59.949
There was something really gorgeous about that.
那真是太美妙了。

00:57:59.949 --> 00:58:04.030
Marshall, you're gonna go back to land and go face the music of actually getting married.
马歇尔，你要回到陆地上，面对真正结婚的音乐。

00:58:04.030 --> 00:58:05.710
It's a great sort of mid-season, right?
这是一个很棒的赛季中期，对吧？

00:58:05.710 --> 00:58:14.230
We're right about at the mid-point, coming up on the mid-point of season two, but it launches, it helps get you into that next push, which is gonna be getting them really married.
我们正处于第二季的中点，即将到来，但它的推出，它可以帮助你进入下一个推动力，这将使他们真正结婚。

00:58:14.230 --> 00:58:15.949
So it's a good one.
所以这是一件好事。

00:58:15.949 --> 00:58:17.309
This is fun to talk about and revisit.
谈论和重温这件事很有趣。

00:58:17.309 --> 00:58:25.150
Just because I'm the resident, since I'm the resident quote guy, I think we can all agree, I'm the resident quote guy.
就因为我是居民，既然我是居民报价员，我想我们都可以同意，我是居民报价员。

00:58:25.150 --> 00:58:26.230
You're the quote guy, sure.
当然，你就是那个引用的人。

00:58:26.230 --> 00:58:27.230
Quote master.
引用大师。

00:58:27.230 --> 00:58:36.789
I think Isaac Dinnison has a line that I've always loved that said the cure for anything is salt water, sweat, tears, or ocean.
我认为艾萨克·丁尼森（Isaac Dinnison）有一句话我一直很喜欢，那就是盐水、汗水、眼泪或海洋是治愈一切的良药。

00:58:36.789 --> 00:58:38.590
That's a great observation.
这是一个很好的观察。

00:58:38.590 --> 00:58:47.690
And I feel, you know, they get, they head to the ocean, but no, you know, normally it's like, you should get in the ocean, but they were just on, they were a top it, and, and they got their, they got their answer.
我觉得，你知道，他们得到了，他们前往海洋，但是不，你知道，通常情况下，你应该进入海洋，但他们只是在上面，他们是最重要的，而且，他们得到了他们的答案。

00:58:47.690 --> 00:58:48.190
Yeah.
是的。

00:58:48.190 --> 00:58:48.690
Yeah.
是的。

00:58:48.690 --> 00:58:49.590
It's our Moby Dick.
这是我们的莫比迪克。

00:58:49.590 --> 00:58:50.789
It's our Moby Dick moment.
这是我们的莫比迪克时刻。

00:58:51.590 --> 00:58:52.590
The wedding is the way to well.
婚礼是走向美好的道路。

00:58:52.590 --> 00:58:53.889
Not, not Moby Dick.
不，不是莫比迪克。

00:58:54.289 --> 00:58:55.190
Not Moby Dick.
不是莫比迪克。

00:58:55.190 --> 00:58:55.789
Hey, yeah.
嘿，是的。

00:58:55.789 --> 00:58:57.090
Not Moby Dick.
不是莫比迪克。

00:58:57.090 --> 00:58:58.590
Oh, it doesn't get any better than that.
哦，没有比这更好的了。

00:58:58.590 --> 00:59:00.090
And that's like a smartless buy.
这就像一次愚蠢的购买。

00:59:00.590 --> 00:59:01.590
Not Moby.
不是莫比。

00:59:02.789 --> 00:59:04.289
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:59:05.239 --> 00:59:06.840
Please equip me.
请装备我。

00:59:07.139 --> 00:59:08.639
